# [[.Name]]

[[.Description]]

Built with the [OTAF rApp SDK](https://pkg.go.dev/[[.SDKModule]]). The SDK owns configuration, the HTTP
surface, ingest, the R1 producer and packaging; this repository owns the
analysis in `internal/logic`.

## Where the logic goes

`internal/logic/logic.go` has three entry points:

| Method | Called when |
| --- | --- |
| `Handle` | a message arrives on any ingest source |
| `Snapshot` | an R1 information job is due for delivery |
| `Register` | the HTTP surface is being assembled |

Everything else is wired in `cmd/[[.Name]]/main.go` and rarely needs changing.

## Onboarding

`[[.Name]]` is deployed by rApp Manager over R1. Build the package and hand it
to the platform:

```bash
rappctl package                 # -> dist/[[.Name]]-[[.Version]].csar
```

Then, against your Non-RT RIC:

1. Push the container image to the registry the chart points at
   (`image.repository` in `deploy/helm/[[.Name]]/values.yaml`).
2. Upload `dist/[[.Name]]-[[.Version]].csar` to rApp Manager and prime it. The
   platform uploads the chart to the chart repository and registers the
   composition, the information type and the service API.
3. Create an rApp instance selecting the resources shipped in the package:

   ```json
   {
     "acm": { "instance": "[[.Name]]-instance" },
     "dme": {
       "infoTypesProducer": ["[[.Name]]-state"],
       "infoProducer": "[[.Name]]-producer"
     },
     "sme": { "serviceApis": "[[.Name]]-api", "providerFunction": "[[.Name]]-provider" }
   }
   ```

4. Deploy the instance. The platform starts the workload and the rApp begins
   answering supervision on `/r1/producer-health`.

Resources are referred to by file base name, so renaming a file under
`rapp-package/Files` changes the identifier the instance must use.

## Configuration

`config/rapp.yaml` is rendered into the deployment by the chart. Any field
carrying an `env` tag can be overridden per environment without a rebuild;
secrets come from the chart's Secret, never from the ACM instance values.

Generate an operator password hash with `rappctl hashpw`.
